cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent Bench"
message: >-
  If you use Agent Bench in your research, teaching, or product evaluation,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Agent Bench is an open-source, framework-first benchmark suite for comparing
  AI agent frameworks side by side. Each framework implements the same
  multi-step task against a shared, versioned fixture set and is scored on two
  equally weighted axes: deterministic task performance and developer
  experience. The harness records reproducible artifacts (agent traces,
  evaluation summaries, and framework evaluations) so that every published
  score can be audited back to the run that produced it.
